%N A398778 Number of irreducible naturally labeled posets on {1,2,...,n}.
%C A398778 A partial order P on [n]={1,...,n} is naturally labeled if x <_P y implies x<y.
%C A398778 A nonempty poset P is irreducible if P=Q(+)R (where (+) denotes the ordinal sum of P and Q) implies that Q or R is empty.
%H A398778 Ricky Ini Liu and Michael Weselcouch, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcta.2019.105136">P-partition generating function equivalence of naturally labeled posets</a>, J. Comb. Theory, Ser. A 170, Article ID 105136 (2020).
%F A398778 a(n) = A006455(n) - Sum_{i=1..n-1} A006455(i)*a(n-i).
%F A398778 G.f.: I(x)=1-1/N(x) where N(x) is the G.f. for the number of naturally labeled posets A006455(n).
%e A398778 For n=3, the irreducible naturally labeled posets consist of the 3-antichain 1+2+3 and the three distinct natural labelings of the poset 2+1: 1<2+3, 1<3+2, 2<3+1 where + denotes disjoint union. Hence a(3)=4.
%Y A398778 Cf. A006455, A323502, A046908, A354615.
